# S1-02 mutation evidence (round-8 remediation snapshot, batch completed 2026-10-24T21:20+08:00)
#
# This file is generated from the two raw runs that are kept as evidence next to it:
#   mutation-batch.py   / mutation-batch.log   42 points (34 named + 8 joint), full output
#   mutation-joint-m26c.py / mutation-joint-m26c.log  three-point joint m26+m28+m33
# The raw logs are the primary record; this file only normalises them into one section per
# point with an explicit denominator and an explicit attribution.
#
# METHOD
#   1. copy CMakeLists.txt + contracts + host + tests into a scratch tree per point,
#   2. apply exactly one textual edit (count(old) must be 1, otherwise PATCH_PATTERN_COUNT),
#   3. configure + build into a separate build directory, run
#      `ctest --output-on-failure` and read the FAIL lines out of THAT SAME ctest stdout
#      (there is no second direct execution of the mutated binary; round-8 N-1 (4)),
#   4. record ctest exit code, FAIL lines and the '(N of M checks failed)' denominator.
#
# TWO CHANNELS, both recorded per point:
#   ctest=N               8 = at least one test failed, 0 = the whole suite stayed green
#   assertion_failures=K  K counts every line starting with 'FAIL ', which includes the
#                         trailing suite summary line 'FAIL storage.<suite> (N of M checks
#                         failed)'. The real assertion count is therefore K-1, and the
#                         per-point counts below are already the K-1 values.
#
# SOURCE_FINGERPRINT (sha256 first 12 hex chars, byte size) of the tree the batch ran on:
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT f9e1964ee544 CMakeLists.txt 3943 B
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT b9ab2abaa41e host/storage/src/repository.c 95832 B
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT 19bd5b4f9e24 host/storage/src/schema.c 26069 B
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT 875036a0abbf host/storage/src/u64.c 2180 B
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT 2229c561f455 host/storage/src/event_key.c 7165 B
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT b01a90e58f18 host/storage/src/regex.c 25127 B
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT f1cc609cf4cf tests/unit/storage/test_repository.c 138538 B
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT 4952adc2876f tests/unit/storage/test_schema.c 31269 B
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT 6919ee375023 tests/unit/storage/test_u64.c 6040 B
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT 159254c9091d tests/unit/storage/test_event_key.c 7913 B
#   SOURCE_FINGERPRINT 8bb903aa8b76 tests/unit/storage/test_regex.c 5128 B
#
# DENOMINATORS: storage.repository 865, storage.regex 46, storage.u64 90, storage.schema 131.
# m9b_doc_bytes reports 850 instead of 865 because its first failing assertion makes the
# page root NULL, so the assertions that need the root are skipped and never counted.
# Line numbers refer to tests/unit/storage/test_*.c unless stated otherwise.
#
# SCOPE: 42 runs = 34 named points + 8 '<name>_plus_ddl_off' joint points. m23/m24 were
# removed earlier as duplicate points (same anchor and same FAIL lines as m17/m18),
# m15_object_type was removed in round 3, and m29b_xinfo_to_info_only was removed in
# round 7 because its edit is byte-identical to m29_table_info: it was a duplicate run,
# not a second defect. None of those are counted here.
#
# NOT CAUGHT, recorded honestly, no assertion invented:
#   m6_sync          PRAGMA synchronous=FULL -> OFF (repository.c:2366). The pragma is
#                    connection-local; no second connection can observe it, so no
#                    assertion is possible from the test process. Code inspection only.
#   m9_page_budget   reserved continuation-key space 192*6+8 = 1160 B -> 8 B
#                    (repository.c:975). The reservation is a conservative margin; the
#                    pagination fixtures never come close enough to the 65535 B page
#                    limit for the smaller reservation to change any result.
#   m17/m18/m20b/m21b/m22/m26/m29/m30  single-point variants masked by the round-7
#                    verify_official_ddl byte-exact CREATE TABLE comparison
#                    (repository.c:2244, called at :2077). That guard runs AFTER the
#                    column, key-index and object-list checks and rejects any database
#                    whose stored CREATE TABLE text is not byte-identical to the single
#                    schema-v1.sql, so disabling one earlier check alone still leaves the
#                    fixture rejected and the suite green. The real order is:
#                    verify_table_columns (:2061) -> verify_key_index (:2065) ->
#                    verify_official_objects (:2071) -> verify_official_ddl (:2077).
#                    The object-list guard is therefore NOT 'before the index check'; it
#                    runs after it and re-rejects the same fixtures. Each masked point has
#                    a joint run below, and the single run is not counted as coverage.
#                    A joint run only shows the behaviour of that branch once the fallback
#                    is disabled; it does not by itself prove the branch is indispensable
#                    while every guard is enabled (round-8 N-1 (3)).
#
# ATTRIBUTION OF THE JOINT RUNS (round-8 audit section 4.3, recomputed from this log).
#   Every joint run also applies m33, so each of them reports the 6 real assertions of the
#   CHECK / FOREIGN KEY / same-length DDL fixtures (:2542 :2543 :2554 :2555 :2567 :2568)
#   and one ':2250 repo == NULL' per rejected fixture. Full decomposition (real
#   assertions = helper :2250 + m33 DDL lines + target-fixture lines):
#     m17+ddl_off  32 = 16 + 6 + 10
#     m18+ddl_off  24 = 12 + 6 +  6
#     m20b+ddl_off 16 =  8 + 6 +  2
#     m21b+ddl_off 16 =  8 + 6 +  2
#     m22+ddl_off  16 =  8 + 6 +  2
#     m26+ddl_off  12 =  6 + 6 +  0
#     m29+ddl_off  16 =  8 + 6 +  2
#     m30+ddl_off  16 =  8 + 6 +  2
#   Equivalently, real minus the 12 lines that m33 itself contributes gives the numbers
#   quoted by the round-8 audit (20/12/4/4/4/0/4/4), which still contain the ':2250'
#   helper line of each target fixture.
#   m26+ddl_off has zero target lines: disabling the partial-UNIQUE check alone still
#   leaves struct_partial.db rejected by the object-list guard, so its 12 lines must NOT
#   be read as partial-UNIQUE coverage.
#   m26b_partial_plus_objects (m26+m28) reports 4 real failures: test_repository.c:2250 x2
#   plus :2475/:2476. Those are the (11) trigger fixture, not struct_partial.db
#   (:2460/:2461), so m26b is NOT evidence for the partial-UNIQUE branch either
#   (round-8 N-1 (1)). The only run that makes the partial branch observable is the
#   three-point joint m26+m28+m33 (kept in mutation-joint-m26c.log): 20 real failures =
#   4 partial (:2250 + :2460/:2461), 4 trigger (:2475/:2476) and 12 from m33.
#
# KNOWN ATTRIBUTION LIMITS (recorded, not hidden):
#   - m17/m18/m20b/m21b/m22/m28/m29/m30/m26b and all 8 joint runs share the fixture
#     open helper at test_repository.c:2250, so each reports 'repo == NULL' once per
#     rejected fixture in addition to the per-fixture status assertion. The counts are
#     the raw per-assertion record, not a de-duplicated behaviour count.
#   - m10/m11 produce chained failures inside one test function; per-case NUL
#     independence is guaranteed by the per-case clean DB fixtures
#     (nul_case_expect_invalid*, test_repository.c:1869-1928, each with revision=1 as
#     its own baseline) and the nul_pos.db positive control, not by revision carry-over
#     from an earlier case.
#   - m8/m15b also hit the bare-metadata-table and documents-view fixtures at the same
#     time because those fixtures reach the same guard decision point.
#   - m20b and m22 are two different edits of the same if-block at repository.c:2010 and
#     produce identical failure sets; they are counted as two runs, not two defects.
#
